{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap, holding and return rules","requirement":"A landlord may not demand or receive security above one month's rent plus the first month's rent, must hold it for the tenant, and must return the balance with an itemized statement within 21 days after the tenant vacates.","key_value":"1 month's rent (2 months' rent for qualifying small landlords); return within 21 days","coverage_conditions":"Applies to security for a residential rental agreement for property used as the tenant's dwelling. Security collected or demanded before July 1, 2024 is excluded from the subdivision (c) limits.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"natural person or LLC in which all members are natural persons, owning no more than two residential rental properties with no more than four dwelling units","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"The subdivision (c) limits do not apply to security collected or demanded before July 1, 2024; an advance payment of six months' or more rent is allowed if the lease term is six months or longer; the small-landlord two-month cap does not apply to service members.","coverage_quotes":["(a) This section applies to security for a rental agreement for residential property that is used as the dwelling of the tenant.","(i) The landlord is a natural person or a limited liability company in which all members are natural persons. (ii) The landlord owns no more than two residential rental properties that collectively include no more than four dwelling units offered for rent.","(6) This subdivision shall not apply to a security collected or demanded by the landlord before July 1, 2024."]},"exemptions":"Security collected or demanded before July 1, 2024; advance payment of six months' or more rent where the lease term is six months or longer; mutual agreements for alterations; small landlords may demand up to two months' rent, except from service members.","penalty":"A landlord who in bad faith fails to comply with the itemized-statement and return requirements of subdivision (h) shall not be entitled to claim any amount of the security; successors in interest are jointly and severally liable for repayment.","effective_date":"2024-07-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(c) (1) Except as provided in paragraph (2), (3), or (5), a landlord shall not demand or receive security, however denominated, in an amount or value in excess of an amount equal to one month’s rent, in addition to any rent for the first month paid on or before initial occupancy.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D025-01","doc_id":"D025","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California tenant-processing charges counted as security","requirement":"A payment, fee, deposit or charge imposed at the start of a tenancy to reimburse the landlord for costs of processing a new tenant counts as 'security', subject to the limits and return rules of this section, except as provided in Section 1950.6.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Applies to security for a residential rental agreement for property used as the tenant's dwelling.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Charges governed by Section 1950.6 (application screening fees).","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Cal. Civ. Code § 1950.5","quoted_span":"(b) As used in this section, “security” means any payment, fee, deposit, or charge, including, but not limited to, any payment, fee, deposit, or charge, except as provided in Section 1950.6, that is imposed at the beginning of the tenancy to be used to reimburse the landlord for costs associated with processing a new tenant","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
